WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:03.537
- I freaking love "Ted Lasso".

00:00:04.463 --> 00:00:05.582
(audience cheers)

00:00:05.582 --> 00:00:06.415
Imma nerd.

00:00:06.415 --> 00:00:07.360
I know everyone says this.

00:00:07.360 --> 00:00:10.550
I'm not original, but it's
just such a great show.

00:00:10.550 --> 00:00:13.360
It's so innovative and different
from all the other shows.

00:00:13.360 --> 00:00:15.880
And it's just a great, it's a good time.

00:00:15.880 --> 00:00:18.320
And I think, especially for
everybody that's just been,

00:00:18.320 --> 00:00:20.910
felt trapped or maybe
having a (beep) year.

00:00:20.910 --> 00:00:22.180
I don't know if you can
say (beep) year on here,

00:00:22.180 --> 00:00:23.429
but I just did.

00:00:23.429 --> 00:00:24.690
- It depends on the year.

00:00:24.690 --> 00:00:26.167
If the year was (beep) enough,
you can say (beep) year.

00:00:26.167 --> 00:00:31.167
- You can label it. But no, and
it's just such a great show.

00:00:31.312 --> 00:00:33.440
I don't know one person
that doesn't like this show.

00:00:33.440 --> 00:00:34.273
How does that feel?

00:00:34.273 --> 00:00:36.730
To be part of such an amazing
show that everyone loves?

00:00:36.730 --> 00:00:38.401
(audience cheers)

00:00:38.401 --> 00:00:40.318
That's gotta feel cool.

00:00:41.350 --> 00:00:44.073
- I mean, it's surprising and awesome.

00:00:44.980 --> 00:00:46.620
- Is it surprising? Y'all
didn't know, you didn't think?

00:00:46.620 --> 00:00:47.730
- No, we thought, you know,

00:00:47.730 --> 00:00:48.790
it was probably gonna be pretty good.

00:00:48.790 --> 00:00:50.690
There sure were a lot of
talented people involved,

00:00:50.690 --> 00:00:53.110
but you know, we've all been fans of shows

00:00:53.110 --> 00:00:55.528
that then got canceled for
reasons we don't understand.

00:00:55.528 --> 00:00:56.361
- Yeah.

00:00:56.361 --> 00:00:58.610
- So we never could've
anticipated, you know,

00:00:58.610 --> 00:01:00.570
that I'd get to come here, first of all.

00:01:00.570 --> 00:01:04.514
- Yas! I would've never
anticipated. I was very excited.

00:01:04.514 --> 00:01:07.520
Well, who inspired your
character, Coach Beard?

00:01:07.520 --> 00:01:08.920
Did you have an inspiration?

00:01:09.920 --> 00:01:11.246
- Several.

00:01:11.246 --> 00:01:14.350
- You lucky man. You had
several people inspire you.

00:01:14.350 --> 00:01:19.216
- I used to work as a
stagehand at my student union,

00:01:19.216 --> 00:01:22.330
Illinois State University in
beautiful, normal Illinois.

00:01:22.330 --> 00:01:25.423
The Bone Student Center, a.k.a The Boner.

00:01:26.638 --> 00:01:28.250
(audience laughs)

00:01:28.250 --> 00:01:31.320
And the guys I worked with
there, who were my bosses,

00:01:31.320 --> 00:01:34.750
we're just all these,
like, wonderfully, laconic,

00:01:34.750 --> 00:01:38.690
very Midwestern, but way
smarter than they let on, guys.

00:01:38.690 --> 00:01:40.300
Who were just very dry, very droll

00:01:40.300 --> 00:01:43.467
and they would just drop in a
nugget when it had to be said.

00:01:43.467 --> 00:01:46.030
Like I remember one guy, he lost his radio

00:01:46.030 --> 00:01:48.210
and just sitting there,
just all squat in the back.

00:01:48.210 --> 00:01:50.180
He lost his radio, someone
had stolen it or whatever,

00:01:50.180 --> 00:01:53.250
and he goes, "Oh no. My nomenclature."

00:01:53.250 --> 00:01:56.790
Like, nomenclature?
We're in normal Illinois.

00:01:56.790 --> 00:01:58.370
Who's saying nomenclature?

00:01:58.370 --> 00:01:59.420
- Droppin' that knowledge.

00:01:59.420 --> 00:02:01.550
- Yeah. So yeah, those guys.

00:02:01.550 --> 00:02:04.030
- I love that. Well, you
guys shoot in London.

00:02:04.030 --> 00:02:06.040
I love London, especially
at Christmas time.

00:02:06.040 --> 00:02:09.328
What's the biggest cultural
difference for you?

00:02:09.328 --> 00:02:11.680
- Well, one's a physical manifestation

00:02:11.680 --> 00:02:13.930
that people make fun of, but it's true,

00:02:13.930 --> 00:02:16.546
is every time I cross
a street, I might die.

00:02:16.546 --> 00:02:18.440
That never goes away.

00:02:18.440 --> 00:02:20.820
I've now spent a year of the
last two years of my life

00:02:20.820 --> 00:02:23.960
in London and everyday,
several times a day,

00:02:23.960 --> 00:02:27.560
I could die the most
awkward, embarrassing death

00:02:27.560 --> 00:02:29.430
that I'll be known for forever.

00:02:29.430 --> 00:02:30.830
And I never, ever get used to that.

00:02:30.830 --> 00:02:32.560
I have to at every intersection, be like--

00:02:32.560 --> 00:02:35.019
(Brendan gasps)

00:02:35.019 --> 00:02:36.490
- Do they just not pay attention?

00:02:36.490 --> 00:02:38.580
- Well, they're just
comin' from the wrong way.

00:02:38.580 --> 00:02:39.770
(audience laughs)

00:02:39.770 --> 00:02:41.980
- Well, it's the right
way where they're at.

00:02:41.980 --> 00:02:43.400
- But we know.

00:02:43.400 --> 00:02:46.510
(audience laughs)

00:02:46.510 --> 00:02:47.363
- But is it?

00:02:48.620 --> 00:02:51.567
So wait, you had a son, well you didn't.

00:02:51.567 --> 00:02:54.767
That've been amazing.
But, congratulations.

00:02:54.767 --> 00:02:58.417
He's one and half now, so that's amazing.

00:02:58.417 --> 00:02:59.759
(audience applauds)

00:02:59.759 --> 00:03:01.485
Are you still getting
used to being a daddy?

00:03:01.485 --> 00:03:06.050
Oh my gosh. Oh my g--look at the glasses.

00:03:06.050 --> 00:03:07.530
You got a little Beatle on your hands.

00:03:07.530 --> 00:03:09.020
It's, like, amazing.

00:03:09.020 --> 00:03:10.470
- He's amazing.

00:03:10.470 --> 00:03:14.190
He was born out there because
the world being what it was,

00:03:14.190 --> 00:03:17.284
we had no other choice
but to have him out there.

00:03:17.284 --> 00:03:18.480
- Wait, so he was born in London?

00:03:18.480 --> 00:03:19.848
- Yeah, yeah.

00:03:19.848 --> 00:03:21.057
- That's cool.

00:03:21.057 --> 00:03:21.890
- While we were filming this last season.

00:03:21.890 --> 00:03:23.180
- He's already cooler than you.

00:03:23.180 --> 00:03:24.339
- Oh yeah.

00:03:24.339 --> 00:03:25.710
(audience laughs)

00:03:25.710 --> 00:03:26.930
And they don't even
give him a passport yet.

00:03:26.930 --> 00:03:28.780
He was born there, but he
can walk around, you know,

00:03:28.780 --> 00:03:29.613
grade school and be like,

00:03:29.613 --> 00:03:32.427
"I was born in London. It's
cool. NBD. Merry-go-round time."

00:03:32.427 --> 00:03:35.020
- "I'm basically amazing.
I'm Colin Firth."

00:03:35.020 --> 00:03:36.340
That's amazing.

00:03:36.340 --> 00:03:39.100
So you became friends with
your co-star, Jason Sudeikis.

00:03:39.100 --> 00:03:42.480
Right? Did y'all, like,
hit it off in Amsterdam?

00:03:42.480 --> 00:03:43.589
Is this what I heard?

00:03:43.589 --> 00:03:46.090
It's a place to become
friends with people I think.

00:03:46.090 --> 00:03:48.860
- Isn't it? We knew each other

00:03:48.860 --> 00:03:50.630
in the Chicago improv scene, basically.

00:03:50.630 --> 00:03:53.100
And then I moved to Amsterdam
to do comedy out there.

00:03:53.100 --> 00:03:54.758
And then he eventually followed.

00:03:54.758 --> 00:03:58.260
And that's when we became,
like, real solid friends.

00:03:58.260 --> 00:03:59.987
And that's where I
started telling him, like,

00:03:59.987 --> 00:04:02.507
"Hey man, soccer doesn't
suck. Check it out."

00:04:03.840 --> 00:04:05.311
And now it's our job.

00:04:05.311 --> 00:04:06.730
(Kelly laughs)

00:04:06.730 --> 00:04:08.180
- And it's the best job ever.

